### Does the presence of the systemctl binary indicate a running systemd?
### Method A = test -x systemctl ; Method B = systemctl is-system-running
### Method C = /run/systemd/system exists ; Method D = /proc/1/comm

DISTRO       methodA     methodB          methodC   methodD     correct
arch         PRESENT     offline          ABSENT    sh          false  
ubuntu2404   ABSENT      n/a              ABSENT    sh          false  
debian13     ABSENT      n/a              ABSENT    sh          false  
fedora42     ABSENT      n/a              ABSENT    sh          false  

### truth: no container runs systemd as PID 1; PID 1 is the probe shell
### therefore methodA (binary) is a false positive wherever the package is installed,
### methodB is 'offline' (a real systemd answer) even though systemd is NOT init,
### methodC is a side effect of the image, and methodD is the only sound test.

### host contrast (systemd really is init there), from 01_probe_host_bash.json:
pid1_comm=systemd pid1_is_systemd=true systemctl=true is_system_running=running
